    "durationMs": 184161,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n- **Schema** — `links` table (unique `code`, `url`, `clicks` default 0, `id` for creation ordering) migrated against MySQL; all DB settings read from `DB_*` env vars, nothing hard-coded.\n- **API** — `POST /links` (auto-generated 6-char codes, custom 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` codes, 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, 409 on duplicate), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with `Location`, atomic `clicks + 1`), `GET /links` (`{items, total}` ascending). Validation failures, missing/invalid url or code, and malformed JSON all return 422 JSON with an `error` field via a custom exception renderer in `bootstrap/app.php`.\n- **Routes** — registered with `apiPrefix: ''`, covering both the spec paths (`/links`, `/r/{code}`) and the `/projects`-prefixed variants mentioned in the environment notes.\n- **start.sh** — runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground, preserving the provided env vars.\n- **README** — endpoint table and a \"Running the server\" section.\n\nI tested the full flow with curl (creation, validation edges, duplicates, redirects, listing order, 404s, 30 parallel creates with zero duplicate codes, no rate limiting), confirmed data and click counts survive a server restart with idempotent migrations, and left the database clean and the server stopped — ready for `sh start.sh`."
